# DEPENDENCIES
- `zpb-ttf`: https://github.com/xach/zpb-ttf

# USAGE
- `ttf2asciiart hello` => ASCII art is written to standard output in a horizontal format.

## FLAGS
- `-f` or `--font` Set the output font. Default is `/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSerif.ttf`. (It's probably included if you're using Ubuntu.)
- `-v` or `--vertical` Output in vertical text.
- `-w` or `--width` Specify the output width. A value of 48.0 or higher is recommended for properly displaying TTF fonts. Default is 48.0.
- `-h` or `--height` Specify the output height. A value of 24.0 or higher is recommended for properly displaying TTF fonts. Since the terminal stretches the height, half the width value might be appropriate. Default is 24.0.

# BUILD
- Run this command. `sbcl --load build.lisp --quit`
- Currently, You can only create executables using SBCL, but that's because I don't know how to create executables for other systems.